    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0340" n="290" xml:id="pg290"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Goschen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In response to the inquiry the British
                    ambassador made of me yesterday, when handing me a memorandum of Lord
                    Kimberley’s views touching the effect of the recent tariff legislation upon the
                    commercial agreements made with the West Indies under section 3 of the McKinley
                    act, I have the honor to say that the sections to which his lordship refers
                    would, upon the new tariff act becoming a law, operate to cancel those
                    agreements.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
